From 0a829310d451175563191e70cb6ae4d827ca24bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:12:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vr: HUD panel (GA2_VR_HUD_PANEL=1, default off): the 2D
 overlay on a flat panel

In stereo 3D scenes the HUD, dialogue box and menus are drawn on a panel at a
fixed distance instead of baked into the eye images at infinity.

- gs_pgs.cpp: a third paraLLEl-GS instance (eyes[2], own device) gets the same
  packets; the eye instances skip UI primitives, it draws only them into an
  RGBA image (Hacks::ui_layer, parallel-gs branch vr-hud). Split only while the
  frame is a stereo frame; frames carry a flag saying they were split, so the
  panel and the baked UI never show together. Snapshots are taken at the game's
  scene -> scanout copy, so a UI image matches the eye frames on screen.
  GA2_VR_HUD_SSAA (default 1; 4 = 1280x960 image, about +1 ms per vsync).
- ga2_vr.cpp: after each eye's scene image, the panel as a quad seen from the
  pose and field of view the frame is submitted with (premultiplied blend,
  alpha 0x80 = 1.0), then the hands. Angular size of the theater screen at
  GA2_VR_HUD_DISTANCE (1.6 m), centre GA2_VR_HUD_HEIGHT (-0.1 m), fixed in the
  play space (GA2_VR_HUD_LOCK=head: with the head pose), GA2_VR_HUD_SIZE and
  GA2_VR_HUD_GAIN. GA2_VR_EYE_SIZE=<w>x<h> sets the swapchain size
  (diagnostics: Monado's simulated headset recommends 320x240).
- GA2_VR_HUD_DEBUG=1 (no headset): scene + UI instances on the desktop, always
  split; GA2_VR_HUD_DUMP=<prefix> writes -scene.png, -ui.png, -comp.png;
  GA2_PERF=1 prints the classifier counters.
- ga2_pgs::takeEyeFrame gets an optional uiSplit out parameter, new
  uiLayer() / takeUiFrame(); ga2_vr setEyeFrame/setUiFrame. No change to
  headers the game code includes (ga2_stereo.h, ps2_runtime.h).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
